Package: qr2l
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.27), libfontconfig1, libx11-6, libice6, libsm6
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Stefano Caronia <stefano.caronia@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/stefanocaronia/qr2l
Description: Minimalistic QR code generator, as a desktop app and a command-line tool
 qr2l creates QR codes from a desktop app (qr2l-gui) or from the command line
 (qr2l). It recognizes what you type (links, email, phone numbers, SMS,
 WhatsApp, WiFi networks, geolocation, contacts and calendar events) and offers
 a form for the types with more fields. Codes can have custom colors and a logo
 in the middle, and are exported as PNG, SVG, PDF, BMP, JPEG, WebP or
 PostScript. The command-line tool also sets the error correction level and
 the module shape.
